<title>JAPAN: Land liquidity news revives bad-loan laden stocks.</title>
<headline>Land liquidity news revives bad-loan laden stocks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in the financial and construction sectors, both groaning under the weight of bad loans, were revived on Tuesday morning by news that the government would draw up a scheme to improve land liquidity by the end of the month, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0049 GMT, the Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd was up 40 yen at 1,300. Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd added 50 yen to 2,020.</p>
<p>General contractor Haseko Corp jumped 13 yen to 230, the sixth-largest percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. Shimizu Corp rose 25 yen to 672.</p>
